  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For MDM2, the 10 percent practical threshold is approximately 0.0269; positive signed values correspond to stronger dependency when the outcome mean is negative. H90 was due its validation response. The independent validation estimate for BRAF V600E and weaker RIT1 dependency among KRAS wild-type cells is -0.0075 with interval -0.0563 to +0.0413; the point estimate is opposite the claim and the interval includes zero and subthreshold values, so I reject and close H90. H49 validation for KRAS mutation and stronger KRAS dependency among TP53-intact cells is +0.0011 with interval -0.0278 to +0.0300; this is null and below the KRAS practical threshold, so I reject and close H49. H108 asks whether CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency among TP53-loss cells. Its discovery estimate was +0.1106 with lower bound +0.0350, above the MDM2 threshold, but the independent validation estimate is +0.1010 with adjusted interval -0.00035 to +0.2023. The validation point remains large and consistent, but the interval fails to exclude null or subthreshold effects and is based on a smaller TP53-loss subset. Therefore the original accept status is not well supported as an independent clinically meaningful association; I change H108 to unresolved and keep it active because it is scientifically important. H96 remains accepted because the TP53-intact CDKN2A-MDM2 association was independently validated, whereas H108 now indicates only suggestive evidence for extension to TP53-loss cells. H103 tests MTAP loss as a co-deletion modifier within TP53-intact CDKN2A-loss cells. The discovery estimate was positive but imprecise, and the independent validation estimate is -0.0996 with interval -0.2653 to +0.0661. The validation point is opposite the registered direction and provides no support for a clinically meaningful MTAP modifier; I reject and close H103. Overall final conclusions in this supplied dataset: supported and independently validated associations are SMARCA4 loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, TP53 loss with much weaker USP7 dependency, KEAP1 loss with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency, MSI-high with much stronger WRN dependency, and CDKN2A loss with much stronger MDM2 dependency specifically in TP53-intact cells. These are robust across many within-dataset subgroups and library or lineage checks. Negative or unsupported findings include BRAF V600E and RIT1, KRAS mutation among TP53-intact cells, NF1 loss among KRAS wild-type cells, MYC-amplification associations for POLR2A and KIF18A, broad EGFR, ERBB2, PIK3CA, STK11, PTEN, and RIT1 bypass tests, and MTAP loss as an MDM2 modifier. Residual uncertainty concerns whether the CDKN2A-MDM2 effect is confined to TP53-intact cells, whether any TP53-loss effect is real but underpowered, and whether technical batch or 9p21 copy-number strata modulate it. The most informative next analyses are H117, which tests CDKN2A loss and stronger MDM2 dependency without TP53 eligibility, and H118, which tests CDKN2A loss among TP53-loss and MTAP-intact cells. H117 will distinguish a broad CDKN2A-MDM2 association from the validated TP53-intact conditional association; H118 will determine whether any apparent TP53-loss effect persists independently of MTAP co-deletion. All claims remain associations in the supplied dataset and should not be interpreted as causal or externally generalizable without additional validation.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 8 synthesize: H90 and H49 independently validate as null/opposite and are rejected. H108 TP53-loss CDKN2A-MDM2 remains suggestive but not independently validated because the adjusted validation interval crosses zero and fails to clear the 10 percent threshold; status changed to unresolved active. H103 MTAP co-deletion modifier validation is opposite the registered direction and is rejected. Core supported validated associations remain: SMARCA4 loss stronger SMARCA2; TP53 loss weaker USP7; KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2; MSI-high stronger WRN; CDKN2A loss stronger MDM2 in TP53-intact cells. Do not interpret as p53-specific causal mechanism; it is an association pattern. Next highest-value analyses are H117 broad CDKN2A-MDM2 without TP53 eligibility and H118 CDKN2A-MDM2 among TP53-loss MTAP-intact cells. H117 should decide whether the CDKN2A effect is general or conditional on TP53-intact status; H118 tests whether apparent TP53-loss effects persist when nearby MTAP co-deletion is absent. Remaining batch and copy-number strata are imprecise and should only be revisited if the broad CDKN2A-MDM2 test is robust."
